      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Metformin remains the foundational first-line therapy for type 2 diabetes, though guidelines from organizations like the American Diabetes Association (ADA) recommend SGLT2 inhibitors or GLP-1 receptor agonists as early or first-line additions or alternatives\u2014particularly for patients with or at high risk for atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease, heart failure, or chronic kidney disease.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "guidelines from organizations like the American Diabetes Association (ADA) recommend SGLT2 inhibitors or GLP-1 receptor agonists as early or first-line additions or alternatives"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Neither class is universally \"better\" as a standalone first-line agent for everyone; the choice depends heavily on individual patient comorbidities and goals.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          2
        ]
      },
